{"id": "swebq0053", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3724476123, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "3d4d39fcc4a346fd8580c0316523f086cfbea87a1efa8a46667c283f61f94b66", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 NVL", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "who will coach carolina panthers in 2013?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0053.wav", "input_sha256": "1d61b992bf0e1d5283da90de5d5069700dd7a009145764f5b7d91849ffddeae9", "input_samples": 46793, "input_s": 2.925, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.9538, "act": 0.9932, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "I'm going to talk about a little bit of the history and then how we coach pan thers in today's 13. So first, some history. Pan thers have been around for a very long time. They were actually one of the original mascots at Florida State University, which is where I went to school. And so they've been around since the 19 50s, but they' ve always been a part of our culture here in Tall ahassee. We have a lot of people who love them because they're just such a unique animal.And so what we do with them now is we try to keep it as natural as possible. So we don't put any kind of equipment on them. We let them run free, and we just kind of guide them along. So we'll take them out into the field, and then we'll use a couple different methods to get them to come over to us, whether that be food or just calling their name.And then once they' re close enough, we can grab them by the scruff of their neck and hold them up high enough so that they can see everything that's going on around them. But other than that, we really try to keep it as natural as possible.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_tim