{"id": "swebq0240", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1583893070, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "3d4d39fcc4a346fd8580c0316523f086cfbea87a1efa8a46667c283f61f94b66", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 NVL", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "where to go in vietnam beaches?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0240.wav", "input_sha256": "9d8d775be4cd69cf969cfc13e5446d6726386dc56d99d13dc3d7f671c177a1f7", "input_samples": 34162, "input_s": 2.135, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.5625, "act": 0.9972, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Vietnam has some amazing beaches, and there are several great places to visit depending on what you're looking for. If you want a more relaxed, less crowded experience, Nha Trang is fantastic with its long stretch of sand and clear water, plus lots of activities like scuba diving and beach bars.For something even quieter, check out the central coast area near Da N ang or Hoi An; places like My Khe Beach are stunning and not as touristy as some other spots. In the south, Phu Quoc Island offers beautiful white-sand beaches and crystal- clear water perfect for swimming or sunb ading.And if you're heading north, Hal imon Bay near Ha Long Bay is also worth considering for its natural beauty. Just remember that many popular beaches can get busy during peak travel seasons, so it might be nice to plan your trip around off-p eak times for a more peaceful experience.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 44, "feed_lag_max_ms": 128, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 172, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttf